  "goodToKnow": "Verweilen means to linger or stay, a literary word: an einem Ort verweilen, and in brochures, Der Platz lädt zum Verweilen ein. In Goethe's Faust, Faust bets Mephisto that he will never say to a moment Verweile doch! du bist so schön! (Stay a while! You are so beautiful!), and if he does, he loses his soul. Die Weile is a while. Not separable: hat verweilt."
